  "issue": 1252,
  "purpose": "Whether numbered lists that docx-markdoc create splits across headings renumber in Word when a clause is inserted in an earlier list, with REF fields to the later clauses following them, while a list that restarts its count stays restarted (#1252).",
  "word": {
    "platform": "Mac",
    "version": "16.114.3"
  },
  "procedure": "`source` was built with `docx-markdoc create --require-pdf` (every check passed, PDF included). The DOCX was staged in Word's sandbox container, opened in the background, and through AppleScript: a clause was inserted by typing a paragraph break and text at the end of the named list item (the new paragraph keeps the item's list formatting, as pressing Return in Word does), `update field` ran on every field, then each list paragraph's `list string of list format` and each field's code and result were read. The document was closed without saving and reopened for each run. `before` is a run with no insertion. `control` repeats the first-list insertion on the pre-fix output of the issue's reproduction (main @ 6d4cd6b5), where each list had its own abstract definition.",
  "finding": "With one shared ordered abstract definition, a continuing list reusing the previous list's w:numId and a restart as a w:num with a level-0 w:startOverride, Word renumbers every later continuing clause after an insertion in the first list (Closing 3-4 -> 4-5, Termination 5 -> 6) and the REF results to them follow after a field update; the restarted Schedule list and the list continuing it keep 1, 2, 3. An insertion in the restarted list renumbers the list continuing it (3 -> 4) and not the first lists. Before any edit, Word's after-update REF results equal the cached results create wrote. In the pre-fix control, the later list kept its start value and two clauses were numbered 3.",
  "source": "---\ntitle: List Continuation Oracle\n---\n\n# LIST CONTINUATION ORACLE\n\n## Purchase\n\n1. Purchase clause one.\n2. Purchase clause two.\n   1. Purchase sub-clause.\n\n## Closing\n\n3. Closing clause. {% #closing-clause %}\n4. Deliveries. {% #deliveries %}\n   1. Officer certificate. {% #officer-certificate %}\n\n## Termination\n\n5. Termination. {% #termination %}\n\n## Schedule\n\n1. Schedule item one. {% #schedule-one %}\n2. Schedule item two. {% #schedule-two %}\n\n## Survival\n\n3. Schedule item three. {% #schedule-three %}\n\nReferences: {% xref to=\"closing-clause\" /%}; {% xref to=\"deliveries\" /%}; {% xref to=\"officer-certificate\" /%}; {% xref to=\"officer-certificate\" number=\"paragraph\" /%}; {% xref to=\"termination\" /%}; {% xref to=\"schedule-one\" /%}; {% xref to=\"schedule-two\" /%}; {% xref to=\"schedule-three\" /%}.\n",
